WEBVTT

00:03.920 --> 00:09.720
So now I'm combining two tables and I want to see in the results only the matching data between two

00:09.760 --> 00:10.440
tables.

00:10.440 --> 00:12.560
Then I go and use the inner join.

00:12.560 --> 00:15.120
We don't have any other type for that, so that's simple.

00:15.120 --> 00:20.280
But now if I want to see everything, all the data, I don't want to miss anything after joining two

00:20.320 --> 00:20.880
tables.

00:20.880 --> 00:22.120
Then I take a different path.

00:22.160 --> 00:26.080
And here I ask myself, is there like one side more important than the other?

00:26.120 --> 00:29.360
Am I interested in all data from one table?

00:29.360 --> 00:30.120
From one side?

00:30.120 --> 00:33.000
Like here we have like a main table or a master table.

00:33.000 --> 00:35.080
Then I go and use the left join.

00:35.080 --> 00:39.040
But if I want to see all the data from all tables in my query, everything.

00:39.040 --> 00:43.720
So there is no one table more important than other, then I go with the full join.

00:43.720 --> 00:45.160
So this is another path.

00:45.160 --> 00:49.320
And now the third path if I'm interested to see only the unmatching data.

00:49.320 --> 00:51.920
So I'm doing some kind of checkups and so on.

00:51.920 --> 00:53.040
And here again the same thing.

00:53.080 --> 00:56.080
Do I want to see the unmatching data from only one side?

00:56.120 --> 00:58.200
There is like one table that is important.

00:58.200 --> 01:00.760
Then I go and use the left anti-join.

01:00.760 --> 01:06.520
So I want to see the unmatching data from one table, and I'm using the other table only for the check.

01:06.520 --> 01:11.720
But in my query, if both of the tables are important, there is no main table and secondary table.

01:11.760 --> 01:12.880
Both are important.

01:12.920 --> 01:15.320
Then I go and use the full Antijoin.

01:15.320 --> 01:16.520
So actually that's it.

01:16.520 --> 01:22.160
This is the decision tree that I follow usually as I'm writing a query and you might ask me how about

01:22.160 --> 01:23.120
the right join?

01:23.120 --> 01:28.040
Well, as you know me, I don't have it at all in my decision tree, so I don't use it at all.

01:28.080 --> 01:33.720
Now, by looking to this, I can tell you if I check most of the queries that I write very often I use

01:33.720 --> 01:38.160
the left join so I can tell you this is my favorite way on how to join tables.

01:38.160 --> 01:39.760
So let me show you exactly why.
